1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,658
Did you know the sky above
us is like a giant

2
00:00:02,658 --> 00:00:04,509
invisible blanket with
different

3
00:00:04,509 --> 00:00:06,509
layers?

4
00:00:06,509 --> 00:00:08,612
Each layer has its own
special job

5
00:00:08,612 --> 00:00:10,612
Let's explore them together!

6
00:00:10,612 --> 00:00:13,018
Right above where we stand
is the troposphere

7
00:00:13,018 --> 00:00:15,121
This is like our playground of
weather

8
00:00:15,121 --> 00:00:15,393
Here

9
00:00:15,393 --> 00:00:17,564
clouds float like fluffy cotton
candies

10
00:00:17,564 --> 00:00:19,030
and rain falls to water the

11
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:21,030
earth

12
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:23,253
It's where planes zoom
through the sky

13
00:00:23,253 --> 00:00:24,336
and birds fly about

14
00:00:24,336 --> 00:00:27,343
It’s as close as a cozy
sweater keeping us warm

15
00:00:27,343 --> 00:00:29,343
Next up is the stratosphere

16
00:00:29,343 --> 00:00:31,343
Imagine this layer as the
protector

17
00:00:31,343 --> 00:00:31,658
Here

18
00:00:31,658 --> 00:00:33,177
we have the ozone layer

19
00:00:33,177 --> 00:00:36,152
like a shield that blocks out
some of the sun’s

20
00:00:36,152 --> 00:00:36,902
strong rays

21
00:00:36,902 --> 00:00:38,152
just like sunscreen!

22
00:00:38,152 --> 00:00:42,060
It’s also home to the
fast-moving jet stream that
helps planes fly quicker

23
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,814
Higher up is the mesosphere

24
00:00:43,814 --> 00:00:45,317
where the air is chilly

25
00:00:45,317 --> 00:00:46,569
like the inside of a

26
00:00:46,569 --> 00:00:48,569
freezer

27
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:51,875
It’s the place where
meteors come zipping in and
burn up

28
00:00:51,875 --> 00:00:53,591
When you see a shooting star

29
00:00:53,591 --> 00:00:55,482
it’s burning in this very
layer!

30
00:00:55,482 --> 00:00:57,033
Then comes the
thermosphere

31
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:57,863
where it's hot

32
00:00:57,863 --> 00:00:59,692
yet feels cold because the air
is

33
00:00:59,692 --> 00:01:01,692
super thin

34
00:01:01,692 --> 00:01:05,236
It’s a light show stage
where colorful auroras
dance in the sky

35
00:01:05,236 --> 00:01:05,900
like magical

36
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,900
lights

37
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,004
It’s also where space
shuttles sometimes fly

38
00:01:10,004 --> 00:01:11,262
Further and further up

39
00:01:11,262 --> 00:01:12,409
we find the exosphere

40
00:01:12,409 --> 00:01:15,415
This layer feels like the outer
courtyard of our earth-home

41
00:01:15,415 --> 00:01:16,561
Satellites orbit here

42
00:01:16,561 --> 00:01:18,385
circling the earth like tiny
moons

43
00:01:18,385 --> 00:01:19,322
helping us talk to

44
00:01:19,322 --> 00:01:21,322
friends far away

45
00:01:21,322 --> 00:01:21,743
Finally

46
00:01:21,743 --> 00:01:23,427
beyond all these layers is
space

